## Exact proposed system: NED, nearest old-empty dispatch

For integers $n\ge1$, $M\ge0$, the finite state set is
$X_{n,M}=\{x\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}^n:\sum_i x_i=M\}$, with labelled cyclic indices.
If every coordinate is positive, hold the state. Otherwise each old positive
coordinate sends exactly one chip to the first old zero clockwise. All sends
are simultaneous. Equivalently, old positive coordinates decrement by one,
and every old zero receives the length of the positive run just before it.
The zero state holds. Conservation and nonnegativity make this a total map.
No sink, clock phase, schedule or variable-length trimming is included.

## Pre-code triage and target

The source discovery points to Cannings--Haigh, *Montreal Solitaire* (1992),
DOI 10.1016/0097-3165(92)90037-U. The survey description has the same positive-run
dispatch primitive on a trimmed line, not this labelled finite ring. Original
publisher body is not yet obtained. This is a source risk, not a novelty claim.

An author deduction predicts an exact all-target predecessor decoder by
directed cycles whose positive integer gaps sum to one circumference. It
implies bijectivity and entrance time zero when $M<n$. For $M\ge n$ no complete
recurrent-core or entrance-clock theorem is proposed. The dense-only-positive
core idea is already false: $(2,1,0)\mapsto(1,0,2)\mapsto(0,2,1)\mapsto(2,1,0)$
at $(n,M)=(3,3)$. The proof file must preserve that counterexample.

Only this candidate receives a pilot. Exactly 33 full original boxes:
$n=1,M=0,1,2$; $n=2,M=0,\ldots,5$; $n=3,M=0,\ldots,6$;
$n=4,M=0,\ldots,7$; $n=5,M=0,\ldots,8$. These contain 1725 states in total.
Enumerate every state and every target; check direct simultaneous dispatch,
mass, functional-graph entrance/period/recurrent data, exact decoded inverse,
all-target fibre census and attained maximum fibres. Output every state's
literal successor, entrance/period, complete actual and decoded fibre, and
every box's extrema and witnesses. Check the low-mass recurrence assertion.
Two actual same-parameter executions and raw-byte comparison; no extension.
Observed cycles/fibre maxima are finite facts, not all-size formulas.

## Desk deductions, not extra candidates/pilots

1. Word recolouring $x_i\mapsto\tau_{x_{i-1},x_{i+1}}(x_i)$, where $\tau_{a,b}$
   swaps distinct colours $a,b$ and is identity for $a=b$. On two colours it is
   exactly $x_{i-1}\oplus x_i\oplus x_{i+1}$, so the binary case is elementary
   rule 150, an excluded finite-linear carrier. The larger alphabet has no
   complete temporal/inverse proof here. No pilot and no renamed admission.
2. Directed-relation unique-two-walk update is exactly the prior UWS/R01 rule
   in `replacement_matchings_incidence/SCOUT.md`: ordered pairs with exactly
   one old length-two walk, allowing loops. The identity adapter on adjacency
   matrices identifies the full total map, not merely an example. No pilot.

The lane has one fresh literal finite-ring definition, not a six-rule slate.
Failure to find three eligible carriers is disclosed and not filled with old
comparison rows. Unresolved temporal/source obligations mean NO_PROMOTION.
